WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.704
Host: Connect the urinary route to its two
renal developmental components.

2
00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:11.862
Guide: Nephrons derived from metanephric
mesenchyme connect to the collecting system
derived from the ureteric bud.

3
00:00:11.862 --> 00:00:18.660
Guide: Urine passes through collecting ducts
to calyces, renal pelvis, ureter and bladder,

4
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.254
Guide: then exits through the urethra.

5
00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:24.423
Host: Which developmental pairing is correct?

6
00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:31.047
Guide: Ureteric bud forms the collecting
system; metanephric mesenchyme forms nephrons.

7
00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:36.915
Guide: Reciprocal interaction between these
tissues connects nephrons to the collecting
system.
